course: dictionary
lesson: 13403
title: A formal word: hereafter
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Hereafter is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in letters, rules, contracts and old writing. Most of the time it means from now on, or from this point on. «Please keep your bag under your seat. Hereafter, the bus driver will check every ticket.» The clue is the word after it: the driver checks tickets starting now, so hereafter means from now on.
explain: Lawyers use hereafter to name someone in a document. «This agreement is between Sam Lee, hereafter called the Tenant.» Sam Lee is called the Tenant from this point on in the document. You do not need to know the whole contract to see what hereafter is doing here.
explain: Hereafter can also be a noun, the hereafter, meaning life after death. «Grandad often talks about the hereafter, the life that comes after we die.» The clue is that he talks about it as a place or a life, not a time on a clock. Many Christians believe in eternal life with God after death, and that is one reason the word is used in church.
explain: In everyday speech, people usually say from now on instead of hereafter. If you swap the word into a sentence and it sounds stiff or like a legal letter, a simpler phrase will almost always fit better.
fact: Hereafter means from now on, or from this point on.
fact: In legal papers, «hereafter called the Buyer» means the Buyer is the name used from that point in the document.
fact: As a noun, the hereafter means life after death.
fact: Hereafter is formal, so people in everyday talk usually say from now on instead.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Hereafter, please keep your bag under your seat.» What does hereafter mean here? | *From now on | In the hall | Yesterday | Long ago
exercise: «The seller, hereafter called the Buyer, agrees to pay.» In this sentence, hereafter means | Under the table | In the shop | Before the sale | *From this point on in this document
exercise: «Grandad often talks about the hereafter.» What does the hereafter mean? | The house he lives in now | Tomorrow's weather | *Life after death | A small village
test: Hereafter is a formal word. In everyday talk, people usually say which phrase instead? | Once upon a time | *From now on | Back then | Far away
test: «Hereafter, the library will close at five.» Which phrase is the best swap for hereafter? | Before the library opens | *From now on | Under the library | In the past
exam: «The lawyer wrote, "Sam Lee, hereafter called the Tenant."» What does this tell the reader? | Sam Lee has died and is in the hereafter | Sam Lee is the lawyer's brother | The lawyer is leaving the room | *The name Tenant is used for Sam Lee from this point on in the document
